Z||000006||Predator||05-26-2001||11:15 AM||||That reminds me of a Console Operator where I used to work at. A batch job failed on our mainframe that was holding up the onlines coming up. She called the programmer oncall so he could dial in and fix it. She kept calling him back every 5 to 10 minutes to get a status. When I read the problem ticket I almost died laughing. She put in the ticket that the programmer was having problems staying logged on to the system. Every time she called him she broke his connection, and he had to redial to get back logged on. He finally told her to quit calling him. It was a few years ago, and I wish I could remember her wording in the ticket, but it was similar to the ones shown here. By the time the programmer got the job fixed he was so pi$$ed off he couldn't see straight, because she could not understand that she was causing him to get knocked off the system  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||LarryB||05-26-2001||11:24 AM||||A really good tier-1 support person usually doesn't remain tier-1 for long.<P>In their defense, excepting for the spelling errors a lot of the time the trouble notes are reporting verbatim what the user is saying.<P>BTW, anyone who has ever worked in tech support might get a laugh out of this if they haven't already seen or heard of it. It was penned by a Kiwi named Simon Travaglia, most of it around 10 years ago.<BR> <A HREF="http://bofh.ntk.net/Bastard.html" TARGET=_blank>http://bofh.ntk.net/Bastard.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||05-26-2001||12:26 PM||||We had a client who submitted a ticket for:<BR>"I can't log on to my NT workstation, because someone else's name is on the top line."<P>Yeesh.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
